    "b-30-state-and-events-events-are-the-handshake-25": {
      "id": "b-30-state-and-events-events-are-the-handshake-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Events are the handshake between workers, the runner, and the sleeping\nscheduler loop.\nA producer writes an event with payload and provenance. The runner handles the\noldest relevant unhandled event by invoking the correct next step. The event is\nmarked handled only after the resulting decision or state transition is stored."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
